<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Sign in with Apple. REQUIRED by App Review 4.8 once Google Sign-In ships:
	     an app offering a third-party/social login must also offer a login service
	     that limits collection to name + email, lets the user keep their address
	     private, and does not track them for advertising. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Associated domains. `webcredentials:` is what binds saved passwords and PASSKEYS to
	     this app: without it a platform-passkey request errors outright, and the
	     `.textContentType(.username)` field in SignInView has no domain to offer credentials
	     for. Apple fetches https://caydexinvest.com/.well-known/apple-app-site-association
	     (served by the backend) and checks it names this Team ID + bundle id.

	     ⚠️ Requires the "Associated Domains" capability on the App ID in the Developer portal.
	     Without it the build FAILS TO SIGN — that is the expected error, not a code problem.

	     ⚠️ The domain is effectively permanent: changing it invalidates every passkey users
	     have enrolled. caydexinvest.com is the committed choice. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>webcredentials:caydexinvest.com</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Time Sensitive Notifications. REQUIRED for the `price_alert` kind, which ships
	     `aps.interruption-level = "time-sensitive"` so a threshold the USER set themselves
	     breaks through Focus and Do Not Disturb. Every other kind is `active` or `passive`
	     and needs nothing here.

	     ⚠️ FAILS SILENTLY WITHOUT THIS. iOS does not error, log, or reject the push — it
	     just downgrades the level to `active`, so the notification arrives normally and is
	     suppressed by Focus exactly like a routine one. There is no runtime signal at all.

	     ⚠️ Requires the "Time Sensitive Notifications" capability on the App ID in the
	     Developer portal as well. The entitlement here is only half of it; a build signed
	     against a profile whose App ID lacks the capability FAILS TO SIGN.

	     Verify: iOS Settings › Notifications › Caydex shows a "Time Sensitive Notifications"
	     toggle ONLY when this entitlement is present in the installed build. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.usernotifications.time-sensitive</key>
	<true/>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<!-- App Group. The ONLY channel between this app and the Movers widget extension.
	     The app fetches (it owns the auth token) and writes a small JSON snapshot into
	     the shared container; the widget reads it and performs no network call and no
	     identity read of its own.

	     ⚠️ That split is deliberate and must not be "simplified" into letting the widget
	     call the API. `.claude/rules/auth.md` §8 makes APIClient the one token source
	     precisely because a Keychain reader and the client deliberately DIVERGE during
	     `.restoring` — a widget reading the Keychain would render real-account content
	     while the app UI says guest, and could never refresh an expired token because
	     refresh is main-actor and lives in the app.

	     ⚠️ There is a second, worse trap: `GuestIdentity` stores the per-install id with
	     NO `kSecAttrAccessGroup`. Adding one so an extension could read it would make the
	     existing read miss, mint a fresh UUID, and silently abandon every current guest's
	     watchlist, portfolios, chats and Learn progress. Do not go down that path.

	     ⚠️ Must be identical in ios-Release.entitlements and in the widget's own
	     entitlements, and registered on BOTH App IDs in the Developer portal.
	     `test_ios_widget_parity.py` fails the build if the three copies drift. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.phan.caydex</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
